.TH "RAPTOR-MCP" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-mcp \- Start the MCP server so an AI assistant can build, validate and simulate models. Options are those of raptor\-studio\-mcp.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor mcp\fR [rest ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start the MCP server so an AI assistant can build, validate and simulate models. Options are those of raptor\-studio\-mcp.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Serve MCP over stdio (what an assistant launches).
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor mcp\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Serve MCP over HTTP on localhost with a bearer token.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor mcp \-\-transport http \-\-port 8765 \-\-token\-file ~/.raptor\-token\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pick a free port; the first line of output is the URL.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor mcp \-\-transport http \-\-port 0 \-\-token\-file ~/.raptor\-token\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
success
.TP
\fB1\fR
runtime error
.TP
\fB2\fR
usage error
.TP
\fB3\fR
model invalid (validation errors)
.TP
\fB4\fR
model refused: a shape Raptor 7 cannot run
.TP
\fB5\fR
timed out or aborted; partial results written
.TP
\fB6\fR
output could not be written
.TP
\fB130\fR
interrupted (Ctrl\-C); partial results written
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_DEBUG\fR
same as \-\-debug
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_DEV_FEATURES\fR
same as \-\-dev\-features
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_CONFIG\fR
path of the settings file (same as \-\-config)
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_WORKSPACE\fR
default for \-\-workspace
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_SEED\fR
salt for every random stream (same as \-\-seed)
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
disable colour output
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME\fR
base directories
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/raptor\-studio/config.toml\fR
settings file (see raptor\-config(5))
.TP
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/raptor\-studio/mcp\fR
default MCP server workspace
